{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"A","amends":"clause","what":"M1's rule that a finding whose detail names no path takes the whole sorted touch set is applied to M2's and M3's rows too, via one helper (receiptPathsOf), whose fallback is the touch set when the row's own path list comes back empty — so the hollow-exam row and the three refuted verdicts can never carry an empty paths either.","why":"The receipt shape in fleet/CONTRACT.md and fleet/facts-block.mjs requires paths to be non-empty for a row to be a receipt at all; M2/M3 draw their paths from the exam landings, which are empty for a task whose Proof names no exam, and a row that silently stopped being a receipt would drop out of every judge's FACTS block with nothing to show for it.","id":"01M2NEBZFM0000C0QD9AFZA35W","ts":1789573594612}
